! OPERATION TERMINATION: a BRANCH ON BIT whose store is suppressed must
! not take its branch either.
!
! THE RULE, Reference Manual p.32 on DS: "When an address alarm is
! caused by a data address used in a store-type operation, indicator DS
! is turned on.  Since this indicator is permanently masked on, storing
! in core storage is always suppressed, AND THE OPERATION IS ALWAYS
! TERMINATED."
!
! The branch is part of the operation.  This model suppressed only the
! STORE until now, and protViolates' own comment has named the gap
! since DS was written -- "a BB whose write is suppressed still
! branches".  This is the block that makes it false.
!
! CORROBORATION FROM THE OTHER DIRECTION, same page.  p.32 on IF: "If
! the branch address of a successful branch operation is such that
! control would pass into a protected area, the entire branch
! operation, including any counting, bit changing, or index alteration,
! is suppressed."  That is a different indicator, but it is the manual
! saying plainly that this machine suppresses a WHOLE branch operation
! rather than only its store.
!
! WEAKER STANDARD: hand-written from p.32, like the DF programs beside
! it.
!
! AND THAT IS NOT FOR WANT OF AN ORACLE -- corrected 2026-09-24.  "No
! listing in this collection tests termination", which this note used
! to say, is FALSE.  jb_ax5b routine 1260 TEST 8B (PDF p.75) errors
! with "-SX ABOVE UB WAS NOT NOPED, DATA WAS STORED WHEN ENABLED.",
! and TEST 8C (pp.76-83) checks suppression for DF and IF under four
! enable/mask conditions.  The deck's own write-up (PDF p.8) says TEST
! 8 checks "THAT CORRECT TERMINATIONS AND SUPPRESSIONS OCCUR".  Those
! are the acceptance tests this block should be checked against; it
! was written before they were found.  See docs/NEXT.md item 2.
!
! WHAT IS AND IS NOT COVERED.  Only BRANCH ON BIT.  The other
! store-type operations -- VFL ST and M+, SX/SV/SC/SR, SVA, CM -- have
! side effects of their own (result indicators, index-result
! indicators, progressive index updates) which p.32's "terminated"
! presumably also suppresses, and NONE of that is implemented or tested
! here.  BB was taken first because its side effect is a BRANCH, which
! the program counter records and a PC check can see.
!
! THE SET-UP STORE HAPPENS DISABLED, because p.32 also says "When the
! interruption system is disabled, address monitoring is ineffective...
! the DS, DF and IF indicators cannot be turned on when the system is
! disabled."  That is what lets the program plant a bit in a word it is
! about to protect.
!
! Instructions: BD, BE, LVI, SV, BB1, BBZ, BZB, B, BEW -- all
! implemented.

        SLC, (8)4100.0
START   BD,  $+.32                   ! disable: monitoring is ineffective
        BB1, PROT.0, $+1.0           ! plant bit 0 of PROT while the store
                                     !   can still land
        BZB, PROT.0, $               ! hang if it did not land
        LVI, $X13, TBL
        SV,  $X13, $IA
        LVI, $X13, PROT
        SV,  $X13, $LB               ! lower boundary := PROT
        LVI, $X13, ABOVE
        SV,  $X13, $UB               ! upper boundary := ABOVE
        BBZ, 3.57, $+1.0             ! control bit := 0: signal INSIDE
        BE,  $+.32                   ! enable: monitoring is now effective
!
! ---- 1. a PURE TEST is not a store-type operation ---------------
!   BB changes nothing, so p.32's "store-type operation" does not
!   describe it and nothing may be terminated: the branch must be
!   taken and DS must stay off, even though the word is protected.
!
!   THIS BLOCK EXISTS BECAUSE ITS INJECTION SURVIVED.  The first
!   version of this program had only the modifying case below, so
!   dropping the mod==00 exemption from the model changed nothing and
!   the test still passed -- a condition asserted in a comment and
!   witnessed by nothing.
        BB,  PROT.0, OK1
        B,   $                       ! hang: a pure test must still branch
OK1     BB,  6.0,  $                 ! hang if DS's routine ran
!
! ---- 2. a MODIFYING one is, and is terminated whole -------------
!   PROT's bit 0 is ONE, so this BBZ would branch to WRONG and would
!   clear the bit.  Both are part of one store-type operation on a
!   protected word, so both must be suppressed and DS must be set.
        BBZ, PROT.0, WRONG
!
!   Reached only if the branch was suppressed -- which is why THIS
!   address, and not the word-6 check below, is what witnesses
!   termination.  The NOPs give the DS interruption its quiescent
!   boundary; see df_data_fetch_alarm.strap's note on why this model
!   takes an interruption later than p.48's instruction boundary.
!   Measured: with no slack at all the check below halted with the
!   branch correctly suppressed and word 6 still zero.
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, 6.0,  $                 ! hang if DS's routine did not run
        BBZ, 6.0,  $+1.0
!
!   ... and the bit change was suppressed too.  Read it back with the
!   system DISABLED, so this check cannot itself signal.
        BD,  $+.32
        BZB, PROT.0, $               ! hang if the bit was cleared
        B,   PASS
WRONG   BEW, $                       ! the branch was wrongly taken
PASS    BEW, $
!
! ---- the monitored area ------------------------------------------
        SLC, (8)4300.0
PROT    DD(BU,64,8), 0               ! == the lower boundary
ABOVE   DD(BU,64,8), 0               ! == the upper boundary, first word out
!
! ---- the interruption table --------------------------------------
!   Word 6 is the marker for the reason storage_protection_boundary
!   gives: it is in p.31's 0-31 carve-out and cannot itself signal.
        SLC, (8)4500.0
TBL     DD, 0
        SLC, (8)4523.0
DSRTN   BB1, 6.0, $+1.0              ! entry 19 = DS
        END, START
